Z||000000||chris6878||10-23-1999||12:10 AM||||Sorry Guys...<BR>Me again   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have 85 fiero.. with V6..<BR>I have the engine back in the car and i am getting ready to put the distributor back in.<BR>I have the the # piston at TDC on the compresion stroke...  (i guess this is the way it should be) ...  when i install the distributor, what direction would the rotor button be facing... ( i was told that it should be pointing towards # 1 piston??)<P>After making sure i get it in right, then i will know where to start with the plug wires on the distributor cap... (dont wont to backfire and mess things up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<P>thanks guys/gals||||reg||5
Z||000001||chris6878||10-23-1999||12:12 AM||||sorry..  thats # "1" piston at TDC||||reg||1
Z||000002||ka4nkf||10-23-1999||09:31 AM||||You Point The Rotor To The Number One Plug Wire. This Should Be About Three Oclock On The Dist. Cap. After You Do This The Dist Will Probalby Not Seat All The Way Down. Next Step Is To Hold The Dist. Down And Turn The Engine Until It Seats.  It Has To Engage In The Oil Pump. Make Sure It Seats All The Way Down.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||10-23-1999||10:02 AM||||Don't crank the engine when you're doing this! You'll lose TDC on number 1 cylinder. Drop the distributor in as close as possible to the position you want until it fully seats and then turn the base of the distributor until the rotor points directly to the number 1 plug wire on the cap. You will still need to time it with a light, but this should be close enough to initially fire the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||10-23-1999||12:19 PM||||(dumb question) but...  which plug on the distributor is for the # 1 wire.. ???||||reg||5
Z||000005||batboy||10-23-1999||01:44 PM||||Here is a diagram scanned in from the Haynes Fiero manual that should help you out. The dark circle is number 1 plug wire. Make sure you are at TDC on #1 cylinder and that the timing marks are lined up on the balancer.<P> <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/ignition.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fastonpumpgas||10-24-1999||09:10 AM||||Dont forget the front of the motor it towards the water pump ||||reg||12
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||10-24-1999||08:08 PM||||In the diagram the arrow points to the front of the car. Dist. R&R and timming is discribed in the Haynes Manual.||||reg||1
Z||000008||JetroGT||10-26-1999||05:11 AM||||If you have got everything correct and it still dosen't fire, then it's out phase 180 degreese. Just crank it over by hand again one more time untill #1 piston is at TDC.||||reg||1
